  "name": "Haltech IO Expander 12 (Box A) \u2014 outputs",
  "direction": "transmit",
  "bitrate": 1000000,
  "note": "The four digital pulsed outputs the ECU commands on an I/O Expander 12, at 50 Hz: a duty cycle and a period each. Both fields arrive UNSET \u2014 choose what drives each output, because which channel belongs on a remote pin is a decision about this car and not something the protocol settles. 100 % is raw 1000, which is the 0xFA in byte 0 a box treats as hard on. If Absent is Send zero, so an output whose channel has nothing to say goes off rather than holding. Box A and Box B are the same protocol with every identifier one apart.",
